IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-common`

-- The compulsory third party (CTP) claim in South Australia: Motor Vehicles Act 1959, Part 4 (the notice of claim and
-- the nominal defendant), the Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013, and the damages rules of the Civil
-- Liability Act 1936, Part 8, for an MVA motor accident, with regs 18-19 of the Civil Liability Regulations 2013.
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE, in the texts' own actors and terms: "the claimant", "the injured person", "the insurer", "the
-- nominal defendant", "the court". The injured person's questions are in voc-seat.l4 and the insurer's in
-- voc-seat-insurer.l4; both IMPORT this module and restate no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Motor Vehicles Act 1959: s 99(3), (3a) (death or bodily injury "caused by or arising out of the use
-- of a motor vehicle"); s 104(1)(a) (what a policy insures); s 115(1), (3), (4) (unidentified vehicle); s 116(1), (2),
-- (4), (5) (uninsured vehicle); s 126A (notice of claim; the insurer's and nominal defendant's duties; the consequences of
-- failing). Motor Vehicles (Third Party Insurance) Regulations 2013: regs 4, 5, 6. Civil Liability Act 1936: s 3(1)
-- (MVA motor accident, prescribed minimum, prescribed maximum, State average weekly earnings); s 51; s 52(1), (3)-(8);
-- s 53; s 54; s 56; s 56A(2), (3), (5)-(9); s 58(1)-(4); s 58B(3) with s 54(3). Civil Liability Regulations 2013: reg 7
-- (an ISV is expressed as a whole number, a fraction of a half or more rounded up), regs 18, 19.
--
-- VERSIONS. Accidents from 1 July 2013 only (see Coverage); the contents of a notice of claim given from 1 November 2021
-- (regs 5 and 6 as amended). Earlier dates answer `not covered`. NOTES.md, findings 21, 22 and 25.
--
-- Edition (all from the Open Australian Legal Corpus, South Australian legislation last collected 2025-03-10; NOT the
-- official texts, and they may be out of date): Motor Vehicles Act 1959 as at 2024-11-07, at
-- ../../../motor-vehicles-act-1959/registers/source-bundle/motor-vehicles-act-1959.txt; Motor Vehicles (Third Party
-- Insurance) Regulations 2013 as at 2021-11-01, at ../../../motor-vehicles-third-party-insurance-regulations-2013/
-- registers/source-bundle/motor-vehicles-third-party-insurance-regulations-2013.txt; Civil Liability Act 1936 as at
-- 2023-06-22, at ../../../civil-liability-act-1936/registers/source-bundle/civil-liability-act-1936.txt; Civil Liability
-- Regulations 2013 as at 2015-10-02, at ../../../civil-liability-regulations-2013/registers/source-bundle/
-- civil-liability-regulations-2013.txt. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (CC BY 4.0).
--
-- NUMBERS THAT ARE INPUTS: the CPI (All groups, Adelaide) figures that index the s 52(3) amounts, the prescribed minimum
-- and maximum and the reg 19 hourly rate; the State average weekly earnings (reg 18: an ABS figure); the injury scale
-- value (ISV), which the court assesses under the Regulations' Part 2 and Schedule 1 (not encoded); every amount the court
-- assesses before the Act's limits apply; the minimum superannuation guarantee percentage (Commonwealth law).
-- NOT ENCODED: the rest of Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act (premiums, approved insurers, the insurer's recovery rights,
-- s 127 medical examinations, s 127A-127C, s 128); s 99(4); the Lifetime Support Scheme (s 58A, s 58(5), (6)); Parts 1-7
-- and 9 of the Civil Liability Act (liability, contributory negligence, Part 5 death claims beyond s 54(3) and s 58B);
-- s 52(2) (the 0-60 scale for injuries that are not from an MVA motor accident); s 55 (the discount rate); s 56A(4) and
-- s 58B(2) (how the court weighs chances); s 57; the Civil Liability Regulations' Parts 2 (beyond reg 7), 4 and 5 and
-- Schedule 1.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. Money is in Australian dollars. Regulative clocks are in days.

§ `The CTP claim -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Coverage -- the 2013 scheme`

-- The Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013, from 1 July 2013, inserted MV Act s 126A, inserted CLA
-- s 52(3)-(8), s 56A and s 58B, and inserted s 58(4)-(6). The two transitional clauses differ:
--   * CLA: Sch 2 cl 21(2) (in the CLA deposit): an amendment "that amends section 52, 58 or 65 ... or ... inserts section
--     56A, 58A or 58B ... does not affect a cause of action, right or liability that arose before the commencement of the
--     amendment". The damages rules here do not apply to an earlier accident.
--   * MV Act: Sch 2 cl 22(2) (in the MV Act deposit): "Section 126A ... applies to any claim made after the commencement of
--     that section (including a claim in relation to a death or bodily injury that results from an accident that occurred
--     before that commencement)". So s 126A does reach a claim made after 1 July 2013 about an earlier accident.
-- The Third Party Insurance Regulations commenced on 1 July 2013. SCOPE CHOICE (finding 22): the CTP part of this
-- encoding is the scheme for accidents from 1 July 2013. An earlier accident answers `not covered` throughout: for its
-- damages because the text says so (cl 21(2)), for its notice because this encoding does not take it in, though cl 22(2)
-- would apply s 126A to a claim made after 1 July 2013.
`the first day of the 2013 scheme` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2013

GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accident is within the 2013 scheme` `the accident day` IF
    `the first day of the 2013 scheme` `is on or before` `the accident day`

§§ `MV Act s 99(3), (3a), ss 115, 116 -- whether the CTP scheme covers it, and who answers the claim`

-- s 99(3): "death or bodily injury will be regarded as being caused by or arising out of the use of a motor vehicle only
-- if it is a direct consequence of -- (a) the driving of the vehicle; or (b) the vehicle running out of control; or (c) a
-- person travelling on a road colliding with the vehicle when the vehicle is stationary, or action taken to avoid such a
-- collision." (3a): not "if the death or bodily injury is caused by a terrorist act". "bodily injury includes mental or
-- nervous shock" (s 99(1)). "motor vehicle" is defined in s 5(1), which is deposited (motor-vehicles-act-1959.txt,
-- s 5 from line 316): "a vehicle that is built to be propelled by a motor that forms part of the vehicle but does not
-- include an electric personal transporter (within the meaning of the Road Traffic (Miscellaneous) Regulations 2014) that
-- may be driven on or over a road in accordance with an approval of the Minister under section 161A of the Road Traffic Act
-- 1961"; "vehicle does not include a vehicle operated on a railway or tramway or a mobile machine controlled and guided by
-- a person walking". The definition turns on one fact the person can state, so whether the thing was a motor vehicle in
-- that sense is asked as that fact, with the definition in the question's @desc (finding 27).
DECLARE `How the motor vehicle caused the injury` IS ONE OF
    `as a direct consequence of the driving of the vehicle`
    `as a direct consequence of the vehicle running out of control`
    `as a direct consequence of a person travelling on a road colliding with the vehicle while it was stationary, or avoiding such a collision`
    `in some other way`

GIVEN how IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury`, `it was a terrorist act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3), (3a))` how `it was a terrorist act` IF
        (NOT (how EQUALS `in some other way`))
    AND (NOT `it was a terrorist act`)

-- s 104(1)(a): a policy insures "in respect of all liability ... in respect of the death of, or bodily injury to, any
-- person caused by, or arising out of the use of, the vehicle in any part of the Commonwealth". s 115(1): where "the
-- identity of the vehicle has not after due inquiry and search been ascertained", the person "may recover by action
-- against the nominal defendant". s 116(1): "uninsured motor vehicle means a motor vehicle in relation to which no policy
-- of insurance as required by this Part is in force", but not (a)-(d) vehicles covered by public liability or other
-- prescribed insurance, nor "(e) a motor vehicle in relation to which there is in force a policy of insurance -- (i) that
-- complies with the law of some other State or Territory". s 116(2): damages for death or bodily injury "arising out of
-- the use of an uninsured motor vehicle on a road" may be claimed "against the nominal defendant".
DECLARE `The vehicle's insurance` IS ONE OF
    `insured under a policy under Part 4`
    `insured under a policy that complies with the law of another State or Territory`
    `covered by other insurance that s 116(1)(a)-(d) accepts`
    `uninsured`
    `not identified after due inquiry and search`

DECLARE `Who answers the claim` IS ONE OF
    `the vehicle's CTP insurer (s 126A(1))`
    `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was not identified (s 115)`
    `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was uninsured (s 116)`
    `not covered: another State's or Territory's CTP insurer, under that law`
    `not covered: the other insurance s 116(1)(a)-(d) accepts`
    `no CTP claim: the injury was not caused by and did not arise out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3), (3a))`
    `no CTP claim: an uninsured vehicle that was not on a road (s 116(2))`
    `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`

DECLARE `The motor accident` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                    IS A DATE
    `how the vehicle caused the injury`          IS A `How the motor vehicle caused the injury`
    `it was a terrorist act`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the vehicle's insurance`                    IS A `The vehicle's insurance`
    `the vehicle was on a road`                  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN m IS A `The motor accident`
GIVETH A `Who answers the claim`
`who answers the CTP claim` m MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accident is within the 2013 scheme` (m's `the day of the accident`))
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    ELSE IF NOT (`is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3), (3a))` (m's `how the vehicle caused the injury`) (m's `it was a terrorist act`))
         THEN `no CTP claim: the injury was not caused by and did not arise out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 99(3), (3a))`
         ELSE CONSIDER m's `the vehicle's insurance`
              WHEN `insured under a policy under Part 4` THEN `the vehicle's CTP insurer (s 126A(1))`
              WHEN `insured under a policy that complies with the law of another State or Territory` THEN `not covered: another State's or Territory's CTP insurer, under that law`
              WHEN `covered by other insurance that s 116(1)(a)-(d) accepts` THEN `not covered: the other insurance s 116(1)(a)-(d) accepts`
              WHEN `not identified after due inquiry and search` THEN `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was not identified (s 115)`
              WHEN `uninsured` THEN
                  IF m's `the vehicle was on a road`
                  THEN `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was uninsured (s 116)`
                  ELSE `no CTP claim: an uninsured vehicle that was not on a road (s 116(2))`

-- The VOCA s 17(5)(c) question, "falls within the ambit of a compulsory third-party insurance scheme covering the motor
-- vehicle (whether the vehicle is in fact insured under the scheme or an action for damages lies against a nominal
-- defendant)". READING: it does when this Part gives a claim against an insurer or the nominal defendant, and when
-- another State's or Territory's policy is in force (its own scheme covers the vehicle; whether that scheme's own test is
-- met is not encoded). Not for an accident before 1 July 2013, which this encoding does not cover.
GIVEN m IS A `The motor accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the injury falls within the ambit of a CTP scheme` m IF
    CONSIDER `who answers the CTP claim` m
    WHEN `the vehicle's CTP insurer (s 126A(1))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was not identified (s 115)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was uninsured (s 116)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `not covered: another State's or Territory's CTP insurer, under that law` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN w IS A `Who answers the claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is against the nominal defendant` w IF
       w EQUALS `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was not identified (s 115)`
    OR w EQUALS `the nominal defendant, because the vehicle was uninsured (s 116)`

§§ `MV Act s 126A(1)-(3), Regulations regs 4-6 -- the notice of claim`

-- Reg 4(1): "A notice of a claim under section 126A(1) of the Act must be given -- (a) in the case of a notice of a claim
-- in relation to an action against the nominal defendant -- as soon as reasonably practicable after it becomes apparent
-- that -- (i) the identity of the relevant motor vehicle is not readily ascertainable; or (ii) the relevant motor vehicle
-- was uninsured; or (b) in any other case -- within 6 months after the relevant motor vehicle accident." The same
-- "as soon as reasonably practicable" notice to the nominal defendant is required by ss 115(3), 116(4), "with a short
-- statement of the grounds". What is reasonably practicable is not a number: the answer names the day it runs from.
`the months to give notice of a claim (reg 4(1)(b))` MEANS 6

DECLARE `Notice deadline` IS ONE OF
    `within 6 months after the accident, that is on or before` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `as soon as reasonably practicable after it became apparent that the vehicle could not be identified or was uninsured, which was on` HAS `the day it became apparent` IS A DATE
    `no notice under s 126A: there is no CTP claim against an insurer or the nominal defendant under this Part`

GIVEN w IS A `Who answers the claim`, `the accident day` IS A DATE, `the day it became apparent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice deadline`
`the time for the notice of claim (s 126A(2)(a), reg 4(1))` w `the accident day` `the day it became apparent` MEANS
    IF `the claim is against the nominal defendant` w
    THEN `as soon as reasonably practicable after it became apparent that the vehicle could not be identified or was uninsured, which was on` `the day it became apparent`
    ELSE IF w EQUALS `the vehicle's CTP insurer (s 126A(1))`
         THEN `within 6 months after the accident, that is on or before` (`the accident day` `plus months` `the months to give notice of a claim (reg 4(1)(b))`)
         ELSE `no notice under s 126A: there is no CTP claim against an insurer or the nominal defendant under this Part`

-- s 126A(2): the notice "(b) must be furnished in a manner and form approved by the Minister; and (c) must set out or be
-- accompanied by -- (i) a statement setting out details of the claim; and (ii) a certificate or opinion as to the nature
-- and probable cause of the death or injury ... provided by a medical practitioner; and (iii) the relevant police report
-- number for any report provided to a police officer under the Road Traffic Act 1961 in connection with the relevant
-- accident; and (iv) such other report or other information ... as may be prescribed by the regulations; and (d) must be
-- accompanied by a statement (in a form prescribed by the regulations) authorising the insurer or the nominal defendant to
-- have access to records and other sources of information relevant to the claim." Reg 5(1): the medical certificate "in a
-- form determined by the CTP Regulator"; reg 5(2): "(a) if the claim includes loss of income or earning capacity --
-- evidence of income or earning capacity, including, for example, relevant payslips, PAYG payment summaries or income tax
-- returns; (b) if the claim includes payment of medical expenses -- evidence of expenses incurred up to the date of the
-- claim ...; (c) if the claim relates to the death of a person and is brought under Part 5 of the Civil Liability Act
-- 1936 -- the certificate of death of that person; (d) if the claimant was injured while driving a motor vehicle -- the
-- claimant's driver's licence number; (e) if the claimant was not driving a motor vehicle when he or she was injured --
-- proof of the claimant's identity". Reg 6: the access authority is "a form determined by the CTP Regulator".
DECLARE `Notice item` IS ONE OF
    `a notice of claim in the manner and form the Minister approves (s 126A(2)(b))`
    `a statement setting out the details of the claim (s 126A(2)(c)(i))`
    `a medical practitioner's certificate or opinion of the nature and probable cause of the death or injury, in the CTP Regulator's form (s 126A(2)(c)(ii), reg 5(1))`
    `the police report number of the report made under the Road Traffic Act 1961 (s 126A(2)(c)(iii))`
    `evidence of income or earning capacity, such as payslips, PAYG payment summaries or income tax returns (reg 5(2)(a))`
    `evidence of the medical expenses incurred up to the date of the claim, such as accounts or receipts (reg 5(2)(b))`
    `the certificate of death (reg 5(2)(c))`
    `the claimant's driver's licence number (reg 5(2)(d))`
    `proof of the claimant's identity (reg 5(2)(e))`
    `a statement in the CTP Regulator's form authorising access to records and other information relevant to the claim (s 126A(2)(d), reg 6)`

DECLARE `What the CTP claim includes` HAS
    `the accident was reported to a police officer under the Road Traffic Act 1961` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim includes loss of income or earning capacity`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim includes payment of medical expenses`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim relates to a death and is brought under Part 5 of the Civil Liability Act 1936` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant was injured while driving a motor vehicle`                       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN item IS A `Notice item`, b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Notice item`
`the notice item` item `only if` b MEANS IF b THEN LIST item ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN c IS A `What the CTP claim includes`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Notice item`
`what the notice of claim must include (s 126A(2), reg 5, reg 6)` c MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (LIST `a notice of claim in the manner and form the Minister approves (s 126A(2)(b))`),
        (LIST `a statement setting out the details of the claim (s 126A(2)(c)(i))`),
        (LIST `a medical practitioner's certificate or opinion of the nature and probable cause of the death or injury, in the CTP Regulator's form (s 126A(2)(c)(ii), reg 5(1))`),
        `the notice item` `the police report number of the report made under the Road Traffic Act 1961 (s 126A(2)(c)(iii))` `only if` (c's `the accident was reported to a police officer under the Road Traffic Act 1961`),
        `the notice item` `evidence of income or earning capacity, such as payslips, PAYG payment summaries or income tax returns (reg 5(2)(a))` `only if` (c's `the claim includes loss of income or earning capacity`),
        `the notice item` `evidence of the medical expenses incurred up to the date of the claim, such as accounts or receipts (reg 5(2)(b))` `only if` (c's `the claim includes payment of medical expenses`),
        `the notice item` `the certificate of death (reg 5(2)(c))` `only if` (c's `the claim relates to a death and is brought under Part 5 of the Civil Liability Act 1936`),
        `the notice item` `the claimant's driver's licence number (reg 5(2)(d))` `only if` (c's `the claimant was injured while driving a motor vehicle`),
        `the notice item` `proof of the claimant's identity (reg 5(2)(e))` `only if` (NOT c's `the claimant was injured while driving a motor vehicle`),
        (LIST `a statement in the CTP Regulator's form authorising access to records and other information relevant to the claim (s 126A(2)(d), reg 6)`))

-- Which version. What a notice must include is the law in force when it is given. Reg 5(1) was inserted, reg 5(2)
-- renumbered and reg 6 substituted by 98/2021 from 1.11.2021 (the deposit's legislative history); the earlier text is not
-- deposited, so a notice given before 1 November 2021 is outside this encoding (finding 25).
`the day the deposited regs 5 and 6 took effect` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 11 2021

DECLARE `Notice contents answer` IS ONE OF
    `the notice of claim must include` HAS `the items` IS A LIST OF `Notice item`
    `not covered: a notice given before 1 November 2021, under the earlier regs 5 and 6 (not deposited)`

GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE, c IS A `What the CTP claim includes`
GIVETH A `Notice contents answer`
`s 126A(2), regs 5, 6 -- what a notice of claim given on a day must include` `the day the notice is given` c MEANS
    IF `the day the deposited regs 5 and 6 took effect` `is on or before` `the day the notice is given`
    THEN `the notice of claim must include` (`what the notice of claim must include (s 126A(2), reg 5, reg 6)` c)
    ELSE `not covered: a notice given before 1 November 2021, under the earlier regs 5 and 6 (not deposited)`

§§ `MV Act s 126A(6), (7), Regulations reg 4(2), (3), ss 115(4), 116(5) -- what follows if the claimant fails`

-- s 126A(6): "If a person fails to comply with a preceding subsection -- (a) the insurer or the nominal defendant (as the
-- case may be) may decline to consider or deal with the claim while the failure continues; and (b) the person is not
-- entitled, until the person complies with the relevant requirements, to commence proceedings or to continue proceedings
-- that have been commenced in respect of the death or injury." (7): subject to the regulations. Reg 4(2): a failure to
-- give the notice within the reg 4(1) time "does not attract the operation of section 126A(6) of the Act if -- (a) the
-- failure ... was occasioned by -- (i) ignorance or mistake of the claimant; or (ii) absence of the claimant from the
-- State; or (iii) inability of the claimant on account of injury; or (iv) inability of the claimant on account of the
-- claimant's legal disability; or (v) other reasonable cause; and (b) the proper assessment of the claim has not been
-- substantially prejudiced." Reg 4(3): "Nothing in section 126A of the Act (or these regulations) affects the ability of
-- a person to commence or continue proceedings once the person has provided the information and statements referred to in
-- subsection (2)(c) and (d) of that section (including after the period referred to in subregulation (1) has expired)."
-- Whether the cause was reasonable and whether the assessment was substantially prejudiced are judgments: INPUTS.
-- READING (finding 11): a notice given late without a reg 4(2) excuse is a failure that cannot be cured, so the insurer may
-- go on declining to deal with the claim; reg 4(3) still lets the claimant sue once (2)(c) and (d) are provided.
DECLARE `Why the notice was late` IS ONE OF
    `it was not late`
    `ignorance or mistake of the claimant`
    `absence of the claimant from the State`
    `inability of the claimant on account of injury`
    `inability of the claimant on account of legal disability`
    `other reasonable cause`
    `none of the reg 4(2)(a) causes`

DECLARE `Compliance with s 126A` HAS
    `the notice was in the manner and form the Minister approves (s 126A(2)(b))`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice set out or was accompanied by everything s 126A(2)(c) and reg 5 require`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was accompanied by the access authority (s 126A(2)(d))`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `why the notice was late`                                                                   IS A `Why the notice was late`
    `the proper assessment of the claim has been substantially prejudiced by the lateness`     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS A `Compliance with s 126A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lateness attracts s 126A(6)` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `why the notice was late`
    WHEN `it was not late` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `none of the reg 4(2)(a) causes` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE c's `the proper assessment of the claim has been substantially prejudiced by the lateness`

GIVEN c IS A `Compliance with s 126A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer or nominal defendant may decline to consider or deal with the claim (s 126A(6)(a))` c IF
       (NOT c's `the notice was in the manner and form the Minister approves (s 126A(2)(b))`)
    OR (NOT c's `the notice set out or was accompanied by everything s 126A(2)(c) and reg 5 require`)
    OR (NOT c's `the notice was accompanied by the access authority (s 126A(2)(d))`)
    OR `the lateness attracts s 126A(6)` c

GIVEN c IS A `Compliance with s 126A`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant may commence or continue proceedings (s 126A(6)(b), reg 4(3))` c IF
        c's `the notice set out or was accompanied by everything s 126A(2)(c) and reg 5 require`
    AND c's `the notice was accompanied by the access authority (s 126A(2)(d))`

-- ss 115(4), 116(5): "Where a claimant fails to give notice of a claim in accordance with the requirements of
-- subsection (3) [(4)], and the court before which the action is brought is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that
-- the defendant has been prejudiced in the conduct of the defendant's defence by that failure, it may, if the justice of
-- the case so requires, dismiss the action." The court's satisfaction is an INPUT; dismissal is a power ("may").
GIVEN `the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied the nominal defendant's defence was prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice of the case requires dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may dismiss the action against the nominal defendant (s 115(4), s 116(5))` `the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable` `the court is satisfied the nominal defendant's defence was prejudiced` `the justice of the case requires dismissal` IF
        (NOT `the notice was given as soon as reasonably practicable`)
    AND `the court is satisfied the nominal defendant's defence was prejudiced`
    AND `the justice of the case requires dismissal`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the claimant, the insurer and the nominal defendant`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule starts. The insurer and the nominal defendant are the claim's respondents
-- (in South Australia the insurers are licensed private insurers; the nominal defendant is appointed by the Minister,
-- s 116A, and its liabilities are paid by the insurers, ss 115(2), 116(6)). s 126A(4)-(5) bind both.
DECLARE `CTP party` IS ONE OF `the claimant`, `the insurer`, `the nominal defendant`

DECLARE `CTP act` IS ONE OF
    `give a notice of claim complying with s 126A(2)` HAS `to` IS A `CTP party`
    `send the claimant a copy of the record or information obtained under the access authority`
    `establish practices and procedures to assist claimants to comply with s 126A`

GIVEN w IS A `Who answers the claim`
GIVETH A `CTP party`
`the respondent to the claim` w MEANS
    IF `the claim is against the nominal defendant` w THEN `the nominal defendant` ELSE `the insurer`

-- s 126A(1): "A person who seeks to make a claim for damages or other compensation in relation to the death of, or bodily
-- injury to, a person for which insurance is provided under this Part must furnish the insurer or the nominal defendant
-- (as the case may be) with a notice of claim that complies with the requirements of subsection (2)", within the reg 4(1)
-- time. Clock starts on the day of the accident (for a nominal defendant claim, on the day it became apparent); the seat
-- works out the days. For a nominal defendant claim the days that were "reasonably practicable" are a judgment: an INPUT.
-- If late with a reg 4(2) excuse, s 126A(6) is not attracted and the notice is still owed, with no time; if late without
-- one, the trace ends in BREACH, which here means s 126A(6) applies (the insurer may decline; reg 4(3) still lets the
-- claimant sue once the (2)(c) and (d) material is provided).
GIVEN `the respondent` IS A `CTP party`
      `days allowed for the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the lateness would be excused under reg 4(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CTP party` `CTP act`
DECIDE `s 126A(1), (2), reg 4 -- the claimant must give the insurer or the nominal defendant a complying notice of claim within the prescribed time` IS
    PARTY  `the claimant`
    MUST   `give a notice of claim complying with s 126A(2)` (EXACTLY `the respondent`)
    WITHIN `days allowed for the notice`
    LEST
        IF `the lateness would be excused under reg 4(2)`
        THEN PARTY `the claimant`
             MUST  `give a notice of claim complying with s 126A(2)` (EXACTLY `the respondent`)
             LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 126A(1): no complying notice of claim"
        ELSE BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 126A(2)(a), reg 4(1): the notice of claim was not given in time and reg 4(2) does not excuse it; the insurer or nominal defendant may decline to consider or deal with the claim (s 126A(6)(a)), though proceedings may be brought once the s 126A(2)(c) and (d) material is provided (reg 4(3))"

-- s 126A(4): "An insurer or the nominal defendant must, within 21 days of receiving any record or other information under
-- subsection (2)(d), send a copy of the report or information to the claimant (or a legal practitioner engaged by the
-- claimant)." Clock starts on the day the record or information is received; one rule for each.
`the days to send the claimant a copy (s 126A(4))` MEANS 21

GIVEN `the respondent` IS A `CTP party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CTP party` `CTP act`
DECIDE `s 126A(4) -- the insurer or nominal defendant must send the claimant a copy of each record it obtains under the access authority within 21 days` IS
    PARTY  `the respondent`
    MUST   `send the claimant a copy of the record or information obtained under the access authority`
    WITHIN `the days to send the claimant a copy (s 126A(4))`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 126A(4): a copy of a record or information obtained under the access authority was not sent to the claimant (or the claimant's lawyer) within 21 days of receiving it"

-- What s 126A(4) and (5) require of the insurer and the nominal defendant, as a list for the insurer's seat.
DECLARE `Respondent's duty` IS ONE OF
    `send the claimant (or the claimant's lawyer) a copy of each record or information obtained under the access authority, within 21 days of receiving it (s 126A(4))`
    `establish practices and procedures designed to assist claimants to comply with s 126A (s 126A(5))`

`the duties of the insurer and the nominal defendant to claimants (s 126A(4), (5))` MEANS
    LIST `send the claimant (or the claimant's lawyer) a copy of each record or information obtained under the access authority, within 21 days of receiving it (s 126A(4))`,
         `establish practices and procedures designed to assist claimants to comply with s 126A (s 126A(5))`

-- s 126A(5): "An insurer and the nominal defendant must establish practices and procedures designed to assist claimants
-- to comply with the requirements of the preceding subsections." No time is stated: a standing duty.
GIVEN `the respondent` IS A `CTP party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `CTP party` `CTP act`
DECIDE `s 126A(5) -- the insurer and the nominal defendant must establish practices and procedures to assist claimants to comply` IS
    PARTY  `the respondent`
    MUST   `establish practices and procedures to assist claimants to comply with s 126A`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 126A(5): no practices and procedures designed to assist claimants to comply with s 126A"

§§ `CLA s 3(1) -- the prescribed minimum and the prescribed maximum`

-- s 3(1) "prescribed maximum means -- (a) in relation to an injury arising from an accident that occurred during 2002 --
-- $2.2 million; or (b) ... in a subsequent calendar year -- a sum (calculated to the nearest multiple of $10) that bears to
-- $2.2 million the same proportion as the Consumer Price Index for the September quarter of the preceding year bears to
-- the Consumer Price Index for the September quarter 2001". "prescribed minimum": the same with $2 750. Consumer Price
-- Index: "all groups index for Adelaide". The figures are INPUTS (accidents in 2013 or later only, here).
DECLARE `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts` HAS
    `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` IS A NUMBER
    `CPI for the September quarter 2001`                            IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the stated sum` IS A NUMBER, cpi IS A `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum for the year of the accident` `the stated sum` cpi MEANS
    `rounded to the nearest multiple of $10` (`the stated sum` TIMES (cpi's `CPI for the September quarter of the year before the accident` DIVIDED BY cpi's `CPI for the September quarter 2001`))

GIVEN cpi IS A `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed minimum (CLA s 3(1))` cpi MEANS `the sum for the year of the accident` 2750 cpi

GIVEN cpi IS A `CPI figures for the prescribed amounts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed maximum (CLA s 3(1))` cpi MEANS `the sum for the year of the accident` 2200000 cpi

§§ `CLA s 52 -- damages for non-economic loss in an MVA motor accident`

-- s 51: Part 8 applies "where damages are claimed for personal injury arising from -- (i) a motor accident (whether caused
-- intentionally or unintentionally)". s 3(1) "MVA motor accident means a motor accident where the motor vehicle is a motor
-- vehicle as defined in the Motor Vehicles Act 1959" (not a train or tram). Every CTP claim here is one.
-- s 52(1): "Damages may only be awarded for non-economic loss if -- (a) the injured person's ability to lead a normal life
-- was significantly impaired by the injury for a period of at least 7 days; or (b) medical expenses of at least the
-- prescribed minimum have been reasonably incurred in connection with the injury."
`the days of significant impairment (s 52(1)(a))` MEANS 7

GIVEN `days the ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired` IS A NUMBER
      `medical expenses reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed minimum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 52(1) threshold is met` `days the ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired` `medical expenses reasonably incurred` `the prescribed minimum` IF
       `days the ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired` AT LEAST `the days of significant impairment (s 52(1)(a))`
    OR `medical expenses reasonably incurred` AT LEAST `the prescribed minimum`

-- s 52(7): "An amount applying under subsection (3) (and followed by the word "(indexed)") is to be adjusted on 1 July of
-- each year, beginning on 1 July 2014, by multiplying the stated amount by a proportion obtained by dividing the Consumer
-- Price Index for the March quarter of that year by the Consumer Price Index for the March quarter 2013 (with the amount so
-- adjusted being calculated to the nearest multiple of $10)." (8): "the amount to be applied with respect to a particular
-- injury is the amount applying under subsection (3) at the time of occurrence of that injury". The CPI figures are
-- INPUTS. An injury from 1 July 2013 to 30 June 2014 takes the stated amounts. Unlike VOCA s 4(2), the proportion is not
-- rounded; each amount is rounded separately.
DECLARE `CPI figures for s 52(7)` HAS
    `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` IS A NUMBER
    `CPI for the March quarter 2013`                                       IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the injury day` IS A DATE, cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 52(7)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 52(7) proportion for an injury on` `the injury day` cpi MEANS
    IF `the year of the last 1 July on or before` `the injury day` LESS THAN 2014
    THEN 1
    ELSE cpi's `CPI for the March quarter of the year of the last 1 July adjustment` DIVIDED BY cpi's `CPI for the March quarter 2013`

GIVEN `the stated amount` IS A NUMBER, `the proportion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 52(7) amount for` `the stated amount` `at` `the proportion` MEANS
    `rounded to the nearest multiple of $10` (`the stated amount` TIMES `the proportion`)

-- s 52(3): "(a) the injured person's total non-economic loss is to be assigned a numerical value (an injury scale value)
-- on a scale running from 0 to 100; (b) in assessing the injury scale value, the court must apply any rules prescribed by
-- the regulations; (c) the damages ... are to be calculated as follows: (i) if the injury scale value is assessed as 31 or
-- less but more than 10 (see subsection (4)) -- by adding to $2 000 (indexed) an amount calculated by multiplying the
-- number by which the injury scale value exceeds 10 by $1 000 (indexed); (ii) ... 45 or less but more than 31 -- by adding
-- to $23 000 (indexed) ... exceeds 31 by $3 000 (indexed); (iii) ... 66 or less but more than 45 -- by adding to $65 000
-- (indexed) ... exceeds 45 by $5 000 (indexed); (iv) ... 78 or less but more than 66 -- by adding to $170 000 (indexed) ...
-- exceeds 66 by $10 000 (indexed); (v) if the injury scale value is assessed as 79 or more -- $300 000 (indexed)." The ISV
-- is the court's (Regulations Part 2, Schedule 1): an INPUT. The bands give no amount for an ISV of 10 or less.
-- Reg 7: "An ISV assessed by a court must be expressed as a whole number (a number having a fraction of half or more being
-- rounded up to the nearest whole number)." So an assessment of 10.5 is expressed as 11 (finding 23). READING: a fraction
-- under a half is dropped (10.4 is 10), the nearest whole number. Reg 7 governs every ISV the court assesses, so it is
-- applied before each test on an ISV (ss 52(3)-(6), 56A(2), 58(4)(a)(i)).
GIVEN isv IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ISV expressed as a whole number (reg 7)` isv MEANS FLOOR (isv PLUS 0.5)

GIVEN isv IS A NUMBER, p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` isv `at` p MEANS
    IF isv AT MOST 31
    THEN `the s 52(7) amount for` 2000 `at` p PLUS ((isv MINUS 10) TIMES `the s 52(7) amount for` 1000 `at` p)
    ELSE IF isv AT MOST 45
         THEN `the s 52(7) amount for` 23000 `at` p PLUS ((isv MINUS 31) TIMES `the s 52(7) amount for` 3000 `at` p)
         ELSE IF isv AT MOST 66
              THEN `the s 52(7) amount for` 65000 `at` p PLUS ((isv MINUS 45) TIMES `the s 52(7) amount for` 5000 `at` p)
              ELSE IF isv AT MOST 78
                   THEN `the s 52(7) amount for` 170000 `at` p PLUS ((isv MINUS 66) TIMES `the s 52(7) amount for` 10000 `at` p)
                   ELSE `the s 52(7) amount for` 300000 `at` p

-- s 52(4): "A person who suffers personal injury arising from an MVA motor accident may only be awarded damages for
-- non-economic loss if the injury scale value ... exceeds 10." (5): "However, a court may award damages ... in a case that
-- would otherwise be excluded by operation of subsection (4) if satisfied -- (a) that the consequences of the personal
-- injury with respect to non-economic loss are exceptional when judged by comparison with other cases involving the same
-- injury; and (b) that the application of the threshold ... would ... be harsh and unjust." (6): the assessment "must be
-- based on an injury scale value that should rarely be more than 25% higher than the injury scale value that applies
-- under subsection (3)(a)". The court's satisfaction and the ISV it bases the assessment on are INPUTS; the bands still
-- give nothing if that ISV is 10 or less (finding 13).
DECLARE `Non-economic loss facts` HAS
    `the day of the injury`                                              IS A DATE
    `days the ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired` IS A NUMBER
    `medical expenses reasonably incurred`                               IS A NUMBER
    `the injury scale value`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the court is satisfied under s 52(5)`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury scale value the court bases a s 52(5) assessment on`     IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Non-economic loss answer` IS ONE OF
    `damages for non-economic loss of` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `none: the s 52(1) threshold is not met`
    `none: the injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(4))`
    `none: the s 52(3)(c) bands give no amount for the injury scale value of 10 or less used under s 52(5), (6)`
    `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    `not covered: an injury scale value must be from 0 to 100 (s 52(3)(a), reg 7)`

-- s 52(3)(a): "a scale running from 0 to 100", on the ISV as reg 7 expresses it.
GIVEN isv IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a value on the injury scale` isv IF
    `the ISV expressed as a whole number (reg 7)` isv AT LEAST 0 AND `the ISV expressed as a whole number (reg 7)` isv AT MOST 100

GIVEN n IS A `Non-economic loss facts`, `the prescribed minimum` IS A NUMBER, cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 52(7)`
GIVETH A `Non-economic loss answer`
`s 52 -- damages for non-economic loss` n `the prescribed minimum` cpi MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accident is within the 2013 scheme` (n's `the day of the injury`))
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    ELSE IF NOT (`is a value on the injury scale` (n's `the injury scale value`))
         THEN `not covered: an injury scale value must be from 0 to 100 (s 52(3)(a), reg 7)`
         ELSE IF NOT (`the s 52(1) threshold is met` (n's `days the ability to lead a normal life was significantly impaired`) (n's `medical expenses reasonably incurred`) `the prescribed minimum`)
              THEN `none: the s 52(1) threshold is not met`
              ELSE IF `the ISV` GREATER THAN 10
                   THEN `damages for non-economic loss of` (`the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` `the ISV` `at` p)
                   ELSE IF NOT (n's `the court is satisfied under s 52(5)`)
                        THEN `none: the injury scale value is 10 or less (s 52(4))`
                        ELSE IF NOT (`is a value on the injury scale` (n's `the injury scale value the court bases a s 52(5) assessment on`))
                             THEN `not covered: an injury scale value must be from 0 to 100 (s 52(3)(a), reg 7)`
                             ELSE IF `the s 52(5) ISV` GREATER THAN 10
                                  THEN `damages for non-economic loss of` (`the s 52(3)(c) amount for an injury scale value of` `the s 52(5) ISV` `at` p)
                                  ELSE `none: the s 52(3)(c) bands give no amount for the injury scale value of 10 or less used under s 52(5), (6)`
    WHERE
        p MEANS `the s 52(7) proportion for an injury on` (n's `the day of the injury`) cpi
        `the ISV` MEANS `the ISV expressed as a whole number (reg 7)` (n's `the injury scale value`)
        `the s 52(5) ISV` MEANS `the ISV expressed as a whole number (reg 7)` (n's `the injury scale value the court bases a s 52(5) assessment on`)

§§ `CLA s 53 -- mental harm`

-- s 53: "(1) Damages may only be awarded for mental harm if the injured person -- (a) was physically injured in the
-- accident or was present at the scene of the accident when the accident occurred; or (b) is a parent, spouse, domestic
-- partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in the accident. (2) Damages may only be awarded for pure
-- mental harm if the harm consists of a recognised psychiatric illness. (3) Damages may only be awarded for economic loss
-- resulting from consequential mental harm if the harm consists of a recognised psychiatric illness." "consequential
-- mental harm means mental harm that is a consequence of bodily injury to the person suffering the mental harm"; "pure
-- mental harm means mental harm other than consequential mental harm" (s 3(1)). Whether the harm is a recognised
-- psychiatric illness is a medical question: an INPUT.
DECLARE `Mental harm facts` HAS
    `the person was physically injured in the accident`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was present at the scene of the accident when it occurred`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm consists of a recognised psychiatric illness`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN h IS A `Mental harm facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 53(1) is met` h IF
       h's `the person was physically injured in the accident`
    OR h's `the person was present at the scene of the accident when it occurred`
    OR h's `the person is a parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of a person killed, injured or endangered in the accident`

-- Pure mental harm: the person was not physically injured, so the harm cannot be a consequence of their bodily injury.
-- READING: a person physically injured has consequential mental harm.
GIVEN h IS A `Mental harm facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages may be awarded for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))` h IF
        `s 53(1) is met` h
    AND (   h's `the person was physically injured in the accident`
         OR h's `the harm consists of a recognised psychiatric illness`)

GIVEN h IS A `Mental harm facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages may be awarded for economic loss from the mental harm (s 53(1)-(3))` h IF
        `s 53(1) is met` h
    AND h's `the harm consists of a recognised psychiatric illness`

-- The answer for an accident. s 53 itself dates from 1 May 2004 (amended 1 June 2007), not from 2013, so for s 53 the
-- 1 July 2013 limit is the encoding's scope only (finding 22), not the text.
DECLARE `Mental harm answer` IS ONE OF
    `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, and for economic loss from it`
    `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, but not for economic loss from it (s 53(3))`
    `no damages for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))`
    `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`

GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, h IS A `Mental harm facts`
GIVETH A `Mental harm answer`
`s 53 -- damages for mental harm` `the accident day` h MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accident is within the 2013 scheme` `the accident day`)
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    ELSE IF NOT (`damages may be awarded for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))` h)
         THEN `no damages for the mental harm (s 53(1), (2))`
         ELSE IF `damages may be awarded for economic loss from the mental harm (s 53(1)-(3))` h
              THEN `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, and for economic loss from it`
              ELSE `damages may be awarded for the mental harm, but not for economic loss from it (s 53(3))`

-- The most that may be awarded under ss 54, 56A, 58 and 58B, or `not covered` for an accident before 1 July 2013: the
-- 2013 amendments to ss 58 and the insertion of ss 56A and 58B "do not affect a cause of action ... that arose before"
-- (LSS Act Sch 2 cl 21(2)); s 54 is older, and is kept to the same date by scope (finding 21).
DECLARE `Damages limit` IS ONE OF
    `the most that can be awarded is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`

§§ `CLA ss 54, 56A -- loss of earning capacity`

-- s 54: "(1) If the injured person was incapacitated for work, damages for loss of earning capacity are not to be awarded
-- in respect of the first week of the incapacity. (2) Total damages for loss of earning capacity (excluding interest
-- awarded on damages for any past loss) are not to exceed the prescribed maximum." s 56A(2): "A person who suffers personal
-- injury arising from an MVA motor accident may only be awarded damages for loss or impairment of future earning capacity
-- if the injury scale value that applies under the regulations in relation to the injury exceeds 7." (3): unless the court
-- is satisfied the consequences "are exceptional" and the threshold "would ... be harsh and unjust" (an INPUT). (5):
-- "Damages awarded for any form of loss or impairment of earning capacity (whether past or future) ... must, after applying
-- a discount rate (if any), and any other principle arising under this Act or at common law, including so as to take into
-- account any actual or presumed contributory negligence, be discounted by a further 20%." READING (finding 14): the
-- s 54(2) cap is a "principle arising under this Act", so it is applied before the further 20%. The court's assessments
-- (after contributory negligence and the s 55 discount rate) are INPUTS.
`the further discount (s 56A(5), s 58B(3))` MEANS 0.2

DECLARE `Earning capacity facts` HAS
    `past loss of earning capacity as assessed`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the part of it for the first week of incapacity`                  IS A NUMBER
    `future loss of earning capacity as assessed`                     IS A NUMBER
    `the injury scale value for earning capacity`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the court is satisfied under s 56A(3)`                            IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN e IS AN `Earning capacity facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages for future earning capacity may be awarded (s 56A(2), (3))` e IF
       `the ISV expressed as a whole number (reg 7)` (e's `the injury scale value for earning capacity`) GREATER THAN 7
    OR e's `the court is satisfied under s 56A(3)`

GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, e IS AN `Earning capacity facts`, `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Damages limit`
`ss 54, 56A -- damages for loss of earning capacity` `the accident day` e `the prescribed maximum` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accident is within the 2013 scheme` `the accident day`)
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    ELSE `the most that can be awarded is` ((`the smaller number of` (`the past part` PLUS `the future part`) `and` `the prescribed maximum`) TIMES (1 MINUS `the further discount (s 56A(5), s 58B(3))`))
    WHERE
        `the past part`   MEANS `the larger number of` 0 `and` (e's `past loss of earning capacity as assessed` MINUS e's `the part of it for the first week of incapacity`)
        `the future part` MEANS IF `damages for future earning capacity may be awarded (s 56A(2), (3))` e THEN e's `future loss of earning capacity as assessed` ELSE 0

-- s 56A(6): "The maximum amount of damages that may be awarded to an employed person for loss ... due to the loss of
-- employer superannuation contributions is the relevant percentage of damages payable for the loss or impairment of the
-- earning capacity on which the entitlement to those contributions is based"; (7) "relevant percentage means the
-- percentage of earnings that is the minimum percentage required by law to be paid as employer superannuation
-- contributions" (Commonwealth law, not deposited: an INPUT); (8), (9): the same for a self-employed person.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `damages for the loss of the earning capacity the contributions are based on` IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Damages limit`
`s 56A(6), (8) -- the most for lost superannuation contributions` `the accident day` `damages for the loss of the earning capacity the contributions are based on` `the relevant percentage` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accident is within the 2013 scheme` `the accident day`)
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    ELSE `the most that can be awarded is` (`damages for the loss of the earning capacity the contributions are based on` TIMES `the relevant percentage`)

-- s 56: "Interest is not to be awarded on damages compensating non-economic or future loss."
`interest may be awarded on damages for non-economic or future loss (s 56)` MEANS FALSE

§§ `CLA s 58, Regulations regs 18-19 -- gratuitous services`

-- s 58(1): damages are not to be awarded "(a) to allow for the recompense of gratuitous services except services of a
-- parent, spouse, domestic partner or child of the injured person". (2): those damages "are not to exceed an amount
-- equivalent to 4 times State average weekly earnings". (3): "However, the court may make an award in excess of the limit
-- ... if satisfied that -- (a) the gratuitous services are reasonably required by the injured person; and (b) it would be
-- necessary, if the services were not provided gratuitously ..., to engage another person to provide the services for
-- remuneration, but, in that event, the damages awarded are not to reflect a rate of remuneration ... in excess of State
-- average weekly earnings." (4): for an MVA motor accident "(a) damages referred to in subsection (1) are not to be awarded
-- unless -- (i) the injury scale value ... exceeds 10; and (ii) the services are provided or to be provided -- (A) for at
-- least 6 hours per week; and (B) for a period of at least 6 consecutive months; and (b) any hourly rate used ... is not to
-- exceed a rate prescribed by the regulations". Reg 19(1): "$25 per hour (indexed)"; (2): adjusted on 1 July each year
-- from 1 July 2014 by the March quarter CPI over the March quarter 2013 (no rounding is stated, so none is applied:
-- finding 15). Reg 18: State average weekly earnings are "the relevant male Full-time Adult Average Weekly Ordinary Time
-- Earnings for South Australia as published ... by the Australian Statistician": an INPUT. The court's (3) satisfaction is
-- an INPUT. READING: the (3) weekly limit is State average weekly earnings for each week of services.
DECLARE `Who gives the gratuitous services` IS ONE OF
    `a parent of the injured person`
    `the spouse of the injured person`
    `the domestic partner of the injured person`
    `a child of the injured person`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Gratuitous services facts` HAS
    `who gives the services`                                IS A `Who gives the gratuitous services`
    `the injury scale value for gratuitous services`                                IS A NUMBER
    `hours of services a week`                              IS A NUMBER
    `consecutive months the services are or will be given`  IS A NUMBER
    `weeks of services claimed`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the hourly rate claimed`                               IS A NUMBER
    `State average weekly earnings`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the court is satisfied under s 58(3)`                  IS A BOOLEAN

`the stated hourly rate (reg 19(1))` MEANS 25
`the minimum hours a week (s 58(4)(a)(ii)(A))` MEANS 6
`the minimum consecutive months (s 58(4)(a)(ii)(B))` MEANS 6
`the weeks of State average weekly earnings (s 58(2))` MEANS 4

GIVEN `the injury day` IS A DATE, cpi IS A `CPI figures for s 52(7)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reg 19 hourly rate for an injury on` `the injury day` cpi MEANS
    `the stated hourly rate (reg 19(1))` TIMES (`the s 52(7) proportion for an injury on` `the injury day` cpi)

GIVEN g IS A `Gratuitous services facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `damages for gratuitous services may be awarded (s 58(1)(a), (4)(a))` g IF
        (NOT (g's `who gives the services` EQUALS `someone else`))
    AND `the ISV expressed as a whole number (reg 7)` (g's `the injury scale value for gratuitous services`) GREATER THAN 10
    AND g's `hours of services a week` AT LEAST `the minimum hours a week (s 58(4)(a)(ii)(A))`
    AND g's `consecutive months the services are or will be given` AT LEAST `the minimum consecutive months (s 58(4)(a)(ii)(B))`

-- s 58(4) was inserted from 1 July 2013 and does "not affect a cause of action ... that arose before" (LSS Act Sch 2
-- cl 21(2)): an earlier accident answers `not covered`, not the s 58(4) thresholds.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE, g IS A `Gratuitous services facts`, `the highest hourly rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Damages limit`
`s 58 -- the most damages for gratuitous services` `the accident day` g `the highest hourly rate` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accident is within the 2013 scheme` `the accident day`)
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    ELSE IF NOT (`damages for gratuitous services may be awarded (s 58(1)(a), (4)(a))` g)
         THEN `the most that can be awarded is` 0
         ELSE IF g's `the court is satisfied under s 58(3)`
              THEN `the most that can be awarded is` ((`the smaller number of` `the weekly amount` `and` (g's `State average weekly earnings`)) TIMES g's `weeks of services claimed`)
              ELSE `the most that can be awarded is` (`the smaller number of` (`the weekly amount` TIMES g's `weeks of services claimed`) `and` (`the weeks of State average weekly earnings (s 58(2))` TIMES g's `State average weekly earnings`))
    WHERE
        `the weekly amount` MEANS g's `hours of services a week` TIMES (`the smaller number of` (g's `the hourly rate claimed`) `and` `the highest hourly rate`)

§§ `CLA ss 54(3), 58B -- a death`

-- s 54(3): "the total amount awarded to compensate economic loss resulting from the death of the deceased person (apart
-- from expenses -- such as funeral expenses -- actually incurred as a result of the death) cannot exceed the prescribed
-- maximum and if before the date of death the deceased person received damages to compensate loss of earning capacity,
-- the limit is to be reduced by the amount of those damages." s 58B(3): damages on "a relevant loss of financial support
-- claim must, after applying a discount rate (if any), and any other principle arising under this Act or at common law,
-- including so as to take into account any actual or presumed contributory negligence, be discounted by a further 20%."
-- READING (finding 14): the cap first, then the 20%. The loss as assessed is an INPUT.
GIVEN `the accident day` IS A DATE
      `loss of financial support as assessed` IS A NUMBER
      `damages for loss of earning capacity the deceased received before death` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Damages limit`
`ss 54(3), 58B -- damages for loss of financial support after a death` `the accident day` `loss of financial support as assessed` `damages for loss of earning capacity the deceased received before death` `the prescribed maximum` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accident is within the 2013 scheme` `the accident day`)
    THEN `not covered: an accident before 1 July 2013`
    ELSE `the most that can be awarded is` ((`the smaller number of` `loss of financial support as assessed` `and` (`the larger number of` 0 `and` (`the prescribed maximum` MINUS `damages for loss of earning capacity the deceased received before death`))) TIMES (1 MINUS `the further discount (s 56A(5), s 58B(3))`))
